Z||000000||Xtreme Fiero's||09-07-2000||06:31 PM||||<BR>I have noticed that when I try to start up my car it will crank very slow. and when it starts i nedd to give it gas to keep it running. when I checked the oil it was a bit low but not to bad (1/2 way down the full area) i added oil and started it up it fred right up no problem and went into a nice idle about 15-30 seconds later the car bogged down and cut off the temp gauge was up near the red. I let the car cool down and then drained the oil out, i filled up the oil to the ADD line and started up the car it started fine and idled perfect 15-30 seconds later when it started to bogg down i added some oil, the idle picked right up after about 1-2 min. of this I began to hear a slight knock from the botom end and i quickly turned it off. Is this the oil pump or is my engine doomed? I plan to put in a new oil pump/pan and new main & rod bearings. would this be a waist of my time or is it worth a shot?||||reg||5
